placeholder for a source file that was not part of the shipped build.

The original project imported this model from roundglasses.blend. The game never loaded the
source at runtime - it loaded the imported scene - and that imported scene was
recovered and is still intact. This placeholder therefore only exists so the
exporter re-emits the `.remap` entry that points at it; Blender is never asked
to open it.

A recovered copy of the model sits next to the project in:
    .assets/game/character/accessories/roundglasses.glb

Put the real source back here with Blender configured in the editor and Godot
will reimport it normally.
